* issue #27 |S22|>1 anomaly probe -- probe_lossy_bcs_125C_1p98V
* Fine-resolution low-band stability/match sweep at the worst pre-match DUT cells.
* DUT: design/netlist/lna.spice sha256
*   151aec66ade8f05257795721527b580014edda14793bdafb2a0816d1a212ec64
* inlined VERBATIM below (klt `**.` netlist escapes stripped; probe edits, if
* any, are marked inline and touch ONLY the inductor-loss resistors Rle/Rlc/Rlb).
* Bench: port sources, gmin/tnom options, mu/k expressions and the 50 Ohm port
* convention are identical to the sp_stab bench of sim/lna-characterization
* (netlist-snapshots/20261116-023212-eacd53a/matched_sp_stab.*); the sweep is
* dec 4000 1e7 3e9 -- 100x the committed bench's point density -- over the
* 10 MHz..3 GHz region where every recorded |S22|/mu anomaly lives (188-600 MHz).
* LOCAL single-corner debug probe on the sweep host (ngspice-47, same build as
* the Spot fleet runner; PDK ihp-sg13g2 0.3.0 at /home/ubuntu/share/pdk).
* NOT a PVT campaign; not generated by lna_variant_campaign.py.
.options gmin=1e-10 tnom=27
.lib /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerHBT.lib hbt_bcs
.lib /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib mos_ff
.temp 125
.subckt lna vdd vss rfin rfout

*.iopin vdd
*.iopin vss
